    'html': '<aside class="warning"><p><strong>BETA</strong> This is a beta version of the document. <a href="#">Send feedback</a>.</p>\n</aside><h1 id="introduction">Introduction</h1>\n<p>Demo documentation site, compiled with Pandora@next.</p>\n<h2 id="1installation">Installation</h2>\n<pre><code class="language-bash">npm i @pandora/cli\n</code></pre>\n<p>Installation will be made available through BAMS as an npm package.</p>\n<p>Only internal users will have access to this library.</p>\n<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>\n<pre><code class="language-console">pn --in-dir --out-dir\n</code></pre>\n<p>Pandora CLI expects two arguments. The first is the relative path to the source input files. The second is the directory of where the documentation bundle should be saved.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-console">pn src dist\n</code></pre>\n<p>An example of this could be a directory called <code>src</code> for the input and <code>dist</code> for the output bundle.</p>\n<h2 id="document-structure">Document Structure</h2>\n<pre><code class="language-md">&lt;!-- \n# Meta tag, used to define the doc type and its properties\ntype: nav | menu | page | template\n# Additional properties specific to &#39;template&#39; document type\nname: beta-notice\n# Additional properties specific to &#39;page&#39; document type\nlocation: /start/installation\ntitle: Installation Guide\ndescription: Step-by-step guid to installing Pandora\nlanguage_tabs: [javascript, typescript]\n --&gt;\n\n# Page Title\n\nSome page content\n</code></pre>\n<p>Documents are created mainly using traditional markdown. However, custom syntax can be used to include additional UI pieces for creating in-depth and engaging documentation.</p>\n<p>Pandora accepts 4 different document types for building documentation.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>menu</td>\n<td>This document type is for generating the navigation menu in the header section of the documentation.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>nav</td>\n<td>This document type is for generating the main navigation for the documentation site. This file defines the structure, labels and links, used to navigate around the documentation. External links are also supported.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>template</td>\n<td>This document type is for creating reusable templates. Templates can also include other templates in their document structure.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>page</td>\n<td>This document type is for generating the actual page content. It&#39;s also responsible for defining the route of the page e.g. <code>/start/installation</code>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id="compiler-gotchas">Compiler gotchas</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Pandora will read all files from the <code>--in-dir</code>. Folder structure and names of the files do not matter.</li>\n<li>Supported file types are Pandora Flavoured Markdown. File extensions should be <code>.md</code>.</li>\n<li>Pandora will generate a web bundle and output it into the specified <code>--out-dir</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n'
