            "html": '<aside class="warning"><p><strong>BETA</strong> This is a beta version of the document. <a href="#">Send feedback</a>.</p>\n</aside><h1 id="pandora-flavoured-markdown-pfm">Pandora Flavoured Markdown (PFM)</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Welcome to the full-blown showcase!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>This is a simple paragraph. This document contains samples of PFM.</p>\n<h1 id="h1-heading">h1 Heading</h1>\n<h2 id="h2-heading">h2 Heading</h2>\n<h3 id="h3-heading">h3 Heading</h3>\n<h4 id="h4-heading">h4 Heading</h4>\n<h5 id="h5-heading">h5 Heading</h5>\n<h6 id="h6-heading">h6 Heading</h6>\n<hr>\n<h2 id="emphasis">Emphasis</h2>\n<p><strong>This text is bold</strong></p>\n<p><strong>This text is bold</strong></p>\n<p><em>This text is italic</em></p>\n<p><em>This text is italic</em></p>\n<p><u>This is inserted text (underline)</u></p>\n<p><del>This text is deleted (strikethrough)</del></p>\n<p><mark>This text is highlighted</mark></p>\n<p>This is a snippet of text which includes <strong>bold</strong>, <em>italic</em>, <u>inserted</u>, <del>deleted</del> and <mark>highlighted</mark> text.</p>\n<p>You can also merge <strong><mark><em><del><u>all of the styles</u></del></em></mark></strong>.</p>\n<h2 id="links">Links</h2>\n<p>Links can either be <a href="/some/path">relative</a>, or, <a href="https://github.com">absolute</a>. Relative paths are always treated as internal, whereas, absolute are treated as external to the document.</p>\n<p>Links can also show tooltips. Here&#39;s one that takes you to <a href="https://www.google.com" title="Google tracks you everywhere">Google</a>.</p>\n<h2 id="images">Images</h2>\n<p><img src="https://picsum.photos/400" alt="Random image"></p>\n<h2 id="partials">Partials</h2>\n<p>Partials are reusable templates of sharable markdown.</p>\n<p><img src="https://picsum.photos/100" alt="Random image">\n<img src="https://picsum.photos/100" alt="Random image"></p>\n<p>If a partial template does not exist, the key will just be removed.</p>\n<h2 id="variables">Variables</h2>\n<p>Variables can be used by wrapping variable names in curly braces.</p>\n<p>Contact support using the following email address: <a href="mailto:&#115;&#117;&#x70;&#112;&#x6f;&#114;&#116;&#64;&#101;&#x6d;&#97;&#x69;&#x6c;&#46;&#99;&#x6f;&#109;">&#115;&#117;&#x70;&#112;&#x6f;&#114;&#116;&#64;&#101;&#x6d;&#97;&#x69;&#x6c;&#46;&#99;&#x6f;&#109;</a>.</p>\n<p>Terms and conditions: An extremely long set of terms and conditions that go on for quite a while and should be inspected by a legal entity.</p>\n<h2 id="code">Code</h2>\n<p>Code can be inline, <code>like this</code>.</p>\n<p>Code &#39;fences&#39;:</p>\n<pre><code>Code goes here...\n</code></pre>\n<p>Syntax highlighting:</p>\n<pre><code class="language-javascript">function log (...args) {\n  console.log(...args);\n}\nlog(&#39;The time is&#39;, new Date().toTimeString());\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-typescript">function log (...args: unknown[]): void {\n  console.log(...args);\n}\nlog(&#39;The time is&#39;, new Date().toTimeString());\n</code></pre>\n<p>Any adjacent code blocks will merge into a tabbed group, as long as global language tabs are not set.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;div id=&quot;msgBox&quot; class=&quot;blue&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;btn&quot;&gt;Tap Me&lt;/button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-css">#msgBox {\n  line-height: 40px;\n  border: 2px solid #888;\n}\n.blue {\n  color: blue;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-js">const btn = document.getElementById(&#39;btn&#39;);\nconst msgBox = document.getElementById(&#39;msgBox&#39;);\nbtn.addEventListener(&#39;click&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  msgBox.textContent = `Tapped button at ${Date.now()}.`;\n})\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="sandbox">Sandbox</h2>\n<p>Sandbox regions take &#39;HTML&#39;, &#39;CSS&#39;, and &#39;JS&#39; source code and render the output into a sandboxed IFrame.</p>\n<code-sandbox hash="b282f70c"><pre><code class="language-html">&lt;div id=&quot;msgBox&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;\n&lt;button id=&quot;btn&quot;&gt;Tap Me&lt;/button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-css">#msgBox {\n  padding: 8px;\n  border: 2px solid;\n  margin-bottom: 1em;\n}\nbutton {\n  background: blue;\n  color: white;\n  border: none;\n  height: 30px;\n  min-width: 50px;\n  padding: 0 12px;\n  cursor: pointer;\n}\nbutton:hover {\n  outline: 1px solid blue;\n}\nbutton:active {\n  background: black;\n  outline: none;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-js">const btn = document.getElementById(&#39;btn&#39;);\nconst msgBox = document.getElementById(&#39;msgBox&#39;);\nbtn.addEventListener(&#39;click&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  msgBox.textContent = `Tapped button at ${Date.now()}.`;\n})\n</code></pre>\n</code-sandbox><p>Compilers can be added later on to support TS, LESS, SCSS etc.</p>\n<h2 id="notices">Notices</h2>\n<p>Short syntax:</p>\n<aside class="info"><p>This is an info notice</p>\n</aside><aside class="warning"><p>This is a warning notice</p>\n</aside><aside class="important"><p>This is an important notice</p>\n</aside><aside class="success"><p>Do this</p>\n</aside><aside class="fail"><p>Don&#39;t do this</p>\n</aside><p>Multiline:</p>\n<aside class="info"><p><strong>Info</strong>:\nThis is an info notice, displayed over multiple lines.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-js">console.log(&#39;hello&#39;);\n</code></pre>\n<p><img src="https://picsum.photos/400" alt="Random image"></p>\n</aside><h3 id="providing-good-typeScript">Providing good TypeScript typings</h3><p>TypeScript will infer the class of an HTML element returned from certain DOM APIs based on the tag name. For example, document.createElement returns an HTMLImageElement instance with a src: string property.</p><h3 id="avoiding-issues-with-class-fields">Avoiding issues with class fields when declaring properties</h3><p> have a problematic interaction with reactive properties. Class fields are defined on the element instance. Reactive properties are defined as accessors on the element prototype. According to the rules of JavaScript, an instance property takes precedence over and effectively hides a prototype property. This means that reactive property accessors do not function when class fields are used. When a property is set, the element does not update.</p><hr><h2 id="lists">Lists</h2>\n<p>Unordered lists are created using <code>-</code>, <code>+</code>, or, <code>*</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>An item</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Another item</li>\n</ul>\n<ul>\n<li>Yet another item</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Ordered lists are created using <code>1.</code>, <code>2.</code>, <code>3.</code> etc.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Item number one</li>\n<li>Item number two</li>\n<li>Item number three</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Numbers do not have to be sequential.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Item number one</li>\n<li>Item number two</li>\n<li>Item number three</li>\n</ol>\n<p>You can start numbering at any point.</p>\n<ol start="88">\n<li> Item number eighty eight.</li>\n<li>Item number eighty nine.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Indent to create nested lists.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Parent<ul>\n<li>Child</li>\n<li>Child</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Parent<ol>\n<li>Child</li>\n<li>Child</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<ol>\n<li><p>Parent\na. Child\nb. Child</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>Parent\nI. Child\nII. Child</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id="tables">Tables</h2>\n<p>Tables are useful to show different types of data.</p>\n<p>By default data is left aligned:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Pandora</td>\n<td>A documentation generator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Alignment</td>\n<td>Left</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align="left">Name</th>\n<th align="left">Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align="left">Pandora</td>\n<td align="left">A documentation generator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align="left">Alignment</td>\n<td align="left">Left</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Right aligned:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align="right">Name</th>\n<th align="right">Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align="right">Pandora</td>\n<td align="right">A documentation generator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align="right">Alignment</td>\n<td align="right">Right</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Center aligned:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th align="center">Name</th>\n<th align="center">Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align="center">Pandora</td>\n<td align="center">A documentation generator</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align="center">Alignment</td>\n<td align="center">Center</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n'
        },
        {
            "location": "./button",
            "title": "Button",
            "description": "",
            "layout": "default",
            "language_tabs": [],
            "html": '<h1 id="button">Button</h1>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button cta &gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button disabled&gt;Disabled&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button toggles active&gt;Toggle&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot;&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot; textpos=&quot;before&quot;&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot;&gt;&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot; transparent&gt;&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<p>Use <code>ef-button</code> for actions in forms, dialogs, etc. with support for different states and styles.</p>\n<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>\n<p><code>ef-button</code> can be used similarly to <code>button</code>. Styling and sizing are managed by the theme but can be customized using CSS.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-css">.large {\n  height: 33px;\n  min-width: 100px;\n  font-size: 140%;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button&gt;Default&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button class=&quot;large&quot;&gt;Large&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="change-styles-and-types">Change styles and types</h2>\n<p> <code>ef-button</code> provides various styles to use for different scenarios, for example, call-to-action, disabled, toggles. To use a style, add its attribute to the <code>ef-button</code>.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button disabled&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button cta&gt;OK&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button cta disabled&gt;OK&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button toggles&gt;Toggle button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="inline-icon">Inline icon</h2>\n<p>To show an icon inside <code>ef-button</code>, use the <code>icon</code> attribute. Supported icons depend on the theme and can be seen on the icons page. Text can be configured to display before or after the icon using the <code>textpos</code> attribute.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot;&gt;&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot;&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot; textpos=&quot;before&quot;&gt;Button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="more-contents-in-button">More contents in button</h2>\n<p>If the button width needs to be fixed, and content requires more than one line, set <code>height: auto;</code> to ensure content displays correctly inside the button.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-css">.lines {\n  height: auto;\n  width: 180px;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot; class=&quot;lines&quot;&gt;Fixed width 180px and more contents in button&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="switching-icon-on-mouse-over">Switching icon on mouse over</h2>\n<p><code>ef-button</code> can display an icon for mouse hover by using <code>hover-icon</code> attribute.</p>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;tick&quot; hover-icon=&quot;cross&quot;&gt;&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n&lt;ef-button icon=&quot;cross&quot; hover-icon=&quot;tick&quot;&gt;&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<h2 id="handling-click-events-on-desktop-and-mobile">Handling click events on desktop and mobile</h2>\n<p><code>ef-button</code> provides events that work on both desktop and mobile. Use <code>tap</code> to ensure that the event will work on different platforms.</p>\n<code-sandbox hash="ac9645b3"><pre><code class="language-javascript">\nconst btn = document.getElementById(&#39;button&#39;);\nbtn.addEventListener(&#39;tap&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  document.getElementById(&#39;text&#39;).textContent = &#39;Got event tap!&#39;;\n});\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-css">.container {\n  display: inline-flex;\n  align-items: center;\n  justify-content: flex-start;\n}\n#text {\n  padding-left: 10px;\n}\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-html">&lt;div class=&quot;container&quot;&gt;\n  &lt;ef-button id=&quot;button&quot;&gt;Tap / Click Me&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n  &lt;span id=&quot;text&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;\n&lt;/div&gt;\n</code></pre>\n</code-sandbox><pre><code class="language-html">&lt;ef-button id=&quot;button&quot;&gt;Click Me&lt;/ef-button&gt;\n</code></pre>\n<pre><code class="language-javascript">const btn = document.getElementById(&#39;button&#39;);\nbtn.addEventListener(&#39;tap&#39;, () =&gt; {\n  document.getElementById(&#39;text&#39;).textContent = &#39;Clicked!&#39;;\n});\n</code></pre>\n<link rel="stylesheet" href="../resources/styles/table-api.css">\n\n<h2 id="properties">Properties</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Property</th>\n<th>Attribute</th>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Default</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>active</code></td>\n<td><code>active</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>An active or inactive state, can only be used with toggles property/attribute</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cta</code></td>\n<td><code>cta</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>Set state to call-to-action</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>disabled</code></td>\n<td><code>disabled</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>Set state to disabled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>hoverIcon</code></td>\n<td><code>hover-icon</code></td>\n<td><code>string | null</code></td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>Specify icon to display when hovering. Value can be icon name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>icon</code></td>\n<td><code>icon</code></td>\n<td><code>string | null</code></td>\n<td>null</td>\n<td>Specify icon to display in button. Value can be icon name</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>textpos</code></td>\n<td><code>textpos</code></td>\n<td><code>&quot;before&quot; | &quot;after&quot;</code></td>\n<td>&quot;after&quot;</td>\n<td>Customises text alignment when specified alongside <code>icon</code> property<br />Value can be <code>before</code> or <code>after</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>toggles</code></td>\n<td><code>toggles</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>Enable or disable ability to be toggled</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>transparent</code></td>\n<td><code>transparent</code></td>\n<td><code>boolean</code></td>\n<td>false</td>\n<td>Removes background when specified alongside <code>icon</code> property</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id="events">Events</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Event</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>active-changed</code></td>\n<td>Dispatched on changing <code>active</code> property state by taping on button when property <code>toggles</code> is true.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n'
        }
    ]
};


